---
name: plan-hardening-iteration
version: 1.0.0
description: One plan-hardening iteration as a bd wisp. The scope and critical passes have no edge between them and run in parallel; the planner's fix step needs both.
format: toml
required_variables:
  - root
  - phase
  - iteration
  - iterations
  - planner
---
{#
Rendered with `sc-compose bead render` (operation render, no bd call) to a
.formula.toml, then created with `bd mol wisp <file>`: phase vapor makes every
step ephemeral, so the steps stay out of `bd ready` (they appear with
`bd ready --mol <wisp> --include-ephemeral`). Each step's description is the
whole instruction for its pass; the dispatch template only claims the step,
prints this description and closes the step.
#}
formula = "plan-hardening-iteration"
description = "Plan hardening of {{{ root }}}: iteration {{{ iteration }}} of {{{ iterations }}}."
version = 1
type = "workflow"
phase = "vapor"

[[steps]]
id = "scope"
title = "{{{ root }}} hardening {{{ iteration }}}/{{{ iterations }}}: plan-scope-reviewer pass"
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:plan-hardening"]
metadata = { pass = "scope", root = "{{{ root }}}", planner = "{{{ planner }}}", iteration = "{{{ iteration }}}" }
description = """
Pass: plan-scope-reviewer. Your review instructions are the agent file
`.claude/agents/plan-scope-reviewer.md`; the planning rules are
`.claude/skills/atm-beads/resources/atm-beads-plan-guidelines.md`.

The plan is the phase root {{{ root }}} and its sprint containers. Read them
with the plan block of your dispatch template.

1. Verify first. For each open `stage:plan-fix` bead under {{{ root }}} whose
   `metadata.pass` is `scope`: close it when the plan now resolves it; leave it
   open, with a note saying what is still wrong, when it does not.
2. Review the whole plan as the agent file says and file every new
   Blocking, Important or Minor finding with the finding block. The planner
   is {{{ planner }}}.
3. Close this step: PASS when no Blocking or Important finding filed by this
   pass is open, FAIL otherwise.
"""

[[steps]]
id = "critical"
title = "{{{ root }}} hardening {{{ iteration }}}/{{{ iterations }}}: critical-plan-reviewer pass"
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:plan-hardening"]
metadata = { pass = "critical", root = "{{{ root }}}", planner = "{{{ planner }}}", iteration = "{{{ iteration }}}" }
description = """
Pass: critical-plan-reviewer, a hostile review. Your review instructions are
the agent file `.claude/agents/critical-plan-reviewer.md`; the planning rules
are `.claude/skills/atm-beads/resources/atm-beads-plan-guidelines.md`.

The plan is the phase root {{{ root }}} and its sprint containers. Read them
with the plan block of your dispatch template.

1. Verify first. For each open `stage:plan-fix` bead under {{{ root }}} whose
   `metadata.pass` is `critical`: close it when the plan now resolves it; leave
   it open, with a note saying what is still wrong, when it does not.
2. Attack the whole plan as the agent file says and file every new finding
   with the finding block. The planner is {{{ planner }}}.
3. Close this step: PASS when no Blocking or Important finding filed by this
   pass is open, FAIL otherwise.
"""

[[steps]]
id = "fix"
title = "{{{ root }}} hardening {{{ iteration }}}/{{{ iterations }}}: planner fixes"
needs = ["scope", "critical"]
assignee = "{{{ planner }}}"
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:plan-hardening"]
metadata = { pass = "fix", root = "{{{ root }}}", planner = "{{{ planner }}}", iteration = "{{{ iteration }}}" }
description = """
Planner {{{ planner }}}: fix the plan. This is iteration {{{ iteration }}} of
{{{ iterations }}}.

In lead adversarial mode, start only after the lead tells you every adversary
task of this iteration has closed.

1. List your open fix beads:
   `bd list --parent {{{ root }}} -l stage:plan-fix --assignee {{{ planner }}} --status open -n 0 --json`.
2. For each one, change the plan beads it names with `bd update` (description,
   design, acceptance criteria, metadata) and add a note to the fix bead:
   `bd update <fix bead> --append-notes "fixed: <what changed, where>"`.
   A finding you reject gets `--append-notes "rebutted: <citation>"`. Rebut a
   finding that adds a state, verb, check, artifact or edge the design does
   not name. Never close a fix bead: the pass that filed it closes it.
3. Re-run `.claude/skills/atm-beads/scripts/validate-plan --phase {{{ phase }}}`
   and fix what it reports. When the plan changed, re-run
   `.claude/skills/sprint-review/scripts/sprint-review --root {{{ root }}}` and
   push the DAG to the plan PR.
4. A FAIL from the critical-plan-reviewer in the last iteration is normal: it
   is an adversarial review. Fix its findings and close this step. Do not add
   an iteration; the final formula's verify step checks the fixes.
5. Close this step when every fix bead has a fixed or rebutted note.
"""
